 Font Mine-Regular.ttf
 To install /home/user/.local/share/fonts/Mine-Regular.ttf as
 /usr/local/share/fonts/Mine-Regular.ttf, vtium-config runs this command:
 sudo vtium-config apply /home/user/.config/vtium/drafts/2026-11-19-1
 File: /home/user/.local/share/fonts/Mine-Regular.ttf
 Folder: your folder
 Face: Mine Regular, version 2.37
 OpenType, outline, proportional
 Covers 3000 characters: Latin.
 Sizes: any size, since it has outlines.
 This font is in your own folder, so vtium cannot use it. Install it as a system font, then
 activate it.
 No look uses it.

 Press Enter to install this font as a system font. vtium-config shows the command and asks before
 it runs it. Esc goes back to the list.







 Install this font as the system font /usr/local/share/fonts/Mine-Regular.ttf? The command shown
 above runs and asks for your password.
